# Technical Investigation Report: Milestone UI-M4 (10-Foot Spatial Focus Standardization)

**Date**: 2026-11-05T03:34:00Z  
**Agent**: Explorer 1 (`explorer_ui_m4_1`)  
**Target Architecture**: LG webOS 8.5.0 (Full HD 1920x1080, Chromium ~108 WAM, aarch64 SoC)  
**Assigned Working Directory**: `/home/prem/webos-projects/cinejoy-webos/.agents/teamwork/explorer_ui_m4_1/`

---

## 1. Executive Summary

Milestone UI-M4 focuses on standardizing spatial D-pad remote control focus states across all interactive components in CineJoy webOS (`com.cinejoy.tv`). The target visual design language is the Google TV / cinema-grade aesthetic derived from `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/`, merged seamlessly with CineJoy's high-contrast brand identity (electric neon lime `#95FF50` and deep obsidian canvas `#04120B`).

Our investigation of `app/css/navigation.css`, `app/css/components.css`, `app/css/layout.css`, and `app/css/tokens.css`, in conjunction with all 24 automated test suites (773/773 passing checks), revealed a critical architectural finding:
- **Stylesheet Cascade Conflict**: In `app/index.html` (lines 9-12), `css/navigation.css` is loaded **after** `css/components.css`.
- `navigation.css` currently contains legacy Milestone 3 focus rules (`border: 3px solid #95FF50 !important`, `scale(1.12)`, `scale(1.15)`, and translucent green backgrounds `rgba(149, 255, 80, 0.25)`).
- Because `navigation.css` rules use `!important`, they **completely override and clobber** modernized focus states defined in `components.css` (such as the 5px pure white halo ring, inverted contrast `#FFFFFF` surface with `#202124` text, and scale 1.08-1.10).
- Furthermore, generic `[data-nav="true"].focused` in `navigation.css` injects a 3px border and 1.08 scale onto non-box components like `#osd-scrubber` (`.osd-progress-track`), causing visual artifacts.

This report documents the empirical audit of all focus selectors across all interactive elements, computes exact WCAG AAA luminance contrast ratios, formulates a zero-reflow GPU compositor acceleration strategy, and delivers concrete, surgical CSS proposals for `navigation.css` and supporting stylesheets.

---

## 2. Stylesheet Cascade & Architecture Audit

### 2.1 Stylesheet Load Order (`app/index.html` lines 9-12)
```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="css/tokens.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="css/layout.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="css/components.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="css/navigation.css">
```
Under W3C CSS Cascading and Inheritance Level 4:
When two rules have equal specificity and both declare `!important`, the declaration appearing later in the document tree wins.
Consequently:
$$\text{Priority: } \text{navigation.css} > \text{components.css} > \text{layout.css} > \text{tokens.css}$$

### 2.2 Empirical Conflict Matrix

