## 5. Mathematical Photometric & Contrast Verification

### 5.1 Color Space Luminance Formulas
Standard sRGB relative luminance ($L$) per WCAG 2.1 §1.4.3:
$$sRGB \to Linear: \quad v = \begin{cases} \frac{c}{12.92} & \text{if } c \le 0.03928 \\ \left(\frac{c + 0.055}{1.055}\right)^{2.4} & \text{if } c > 0.03928 \end{cases}$$
$$L = 0.2126 \cdot R_{lin} + 0.7152 \cdot G_{lin} + 0.0722 \cdot B_{lin}$$
$$\text{Contrast Ratio: } CR = \frac{L_1 + 0.05}{L_2 + 0.05} \quad (L_1 > L_2)$$

### 5.2 Verification Calculations
1. **Inverted Contrast (White `#FFFFFF` on Dark `#202124`)**:
   - $R_{dark} = 32 \implies 0.01438$
   - $G_{dark} = 33 \implies 0.01548$
